From f0b9ee6fcc3e51edfb04e2592276a0dabed328d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:44:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/28] Fix function pointer members of global structs

Backport of the GlobalAnalyzer part of
3efe094c8e941d600cd13e0fd50c7557287d95ad (branch fix/fnptr-member, on
upstream main 4da3147) to v1.32.273.

Only the missing call edge is ported.  The rest of the upstream commit
(Declaration::RefDeclaration and its use in InterCodeGenerator and
FunctionSets) fixes a regression of 349b10a, which takes a function
pointer's type from its declaration; v1.32.273 has neither FunctionSets
nor that regression, and RefDeclaration is not needed here: the folded
expression's own type (exp->mDecType) is the member's type, nothing
rewrites it later.  Upstream's IsFunctionType() does not exist in
v1.32.273, so the condition is written out.

v1.32.273 has the same unwrapping: GlobalAnalyzer::Analyze's EX_VARIABLE
case walks a DT_VARIABLE_REF (the parser's constant fold of w.fn, s[1].fn,
o.in.fn, w.arr[1] and tab[1] for global aggregates) to the root variable
and returns that, so EX_CALL's RegisterCall(procDec, w) finds a struct
type and records no call, and the parameter walk that follows runs over
the struct's members instead of the parameters.  Without the edge the
native code generator treats the caller as a leaf and places the callee's
frame over the caller's live locals: wrong code at every native level,
-O0 included, which nethack64 hits with every window call
((*windowprocs.win_putstr)(...), 44 macros in winprocs.h).  The variable's
own analysis (aliasing, DTF_ANALYZED, AnalyzeGlobalVariable) is unchanged
and the function type is returned only for function (pointer) members, so
every other EX_VARIABLE keeps returning the variable.

Upstream's funcptrmembertest.c and funcptrmemberaddrtest.c both crash
v1.32.273's compiler (a call through an array member with a variable
index, and a pointer to a function pointer, both fixed upstream
separately), so autotest/funcptrmembercalltest.c is a reduced test with
the call edge part of funcptrmembertest.c: calls through a global struct
member, (*w.fn)(), an element of a global array of structs, a nested
member, an array member with a constant index and a constant index into a
global array of function pointers, with a plain global function pointer
and p->fn as controls.  It fails with v1.32.273 in the five native
configurations and passes with this change, as do nethack64's
tests/oscar64-repros/r23_call_through_global_struct_member.c and the
probes cg01 and cg04-cg07 of the upstream review (cg02 and cg03 are the
controls and pass before and after).

